<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"> <head> <meta charset="utf-8"> <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=yes" name="viewport"> <title>references</title> </head> <body> <main> <h1 id="sec:citation">1 Citation smoke case</h1> <p>Prior work established the baseline method <span data-cites="alpha2020">[<a href="#ref-alpha2020" role="doc-biblioref">1</a>]</span> and later studies extended it <span data-cites="beta2021 gamma2022">[<a href="#ref-beta2021" role="doc-biblioref">2</a>,<a href="#ref-gamma2022" role="doc-biblioref">3</a>]</span>. The bibliography should be emitted in the generated document, and the author-only citation <span data-cites="alpha2020">[<a href="#ref-alpha2020" role="doc-biblioref">1</a>]</span> should render too.</p> <h1 id="bibliography">References</h1> <div data-entry-spacing="0" id="refs" role="list"> <div id="ref-alpha2020" role="listitem"> <div>[1] </div> <div>Alpha A. A reproducible baseline. Snapshot Journal 2020;1:1–4.</div> </div> <div id="ref-beta2021" role="listitem"> <div>[2] </div> <div>Beta B. A follow-up study. Snapshot Journal 2021;2:5–8.</div> </div> <div id="ref-gamma2022" role="listitem"> <div>[3] </div> <div>Gamma G. A comparative evaluation. Snapshot Journal 2022;3:9–12.</div> </div> </div> </main> </body> </html>
